/* PrismNet SMB client: mount a Windows, macOS, NAS or Samba share as an
 * Amiga volume (SMB 2.0.2 to 3.1.1).
 *
 * 1. Change the Startup line below: the server (name or address), a slash,
 *    then the share, e.g. "nas.lan/public VOLUME=NAS USER=amiga".
 *    PrismNet Prefs (Shares tab) can write this file for you, with
 *    Browse... to pick the share from the server's list.
 * 2. Double-click this icon, or type:  Mount SYS:Storage/DOSDrivers/PSMB0
 *    Drag it into DEVS:DOSDrivers to mount it at every boot (it connects
 *    only when the volume is first used).
 * 3. Unmount with:  ShareUnmount PSMB0:
 *
 * The first time a share with USER= is used, a small window asks for the
 * password once and remembers it (ENVARC:PrismNet/smb/). List a server's
 * shares with:  SMBShares nas.lan USER=amiga
 *
 * Options after the share:
 *   VOLUME=name      volume name on Workbench (default: the share name)
 *   USER=name        account on the server (asks for the password once)
 *   DOMAIN=name      domain or workgroup (default: none)
 *   GUEST            connect without an account
 *   PASSWORD=secret  give the password here instead of the window
 *   TZ=+H[:MM]       time zone, hours east of UTC (default: from Locale)
 *   READONLY         never write
 *   SIGN=AUTO|YES    sign only when the server asks (default), or always
 *   ENCRYPT=AUTO|YES|NO  encrypt when the share demands it (default AUTO)
 *   MAXPROTO=2.0.2|2.1|3.0|3.0.2|3.1.1  highest dialect (default 3.1.1)
 *   IDLE=s           disconnect after s quiet seconds, 0 = never (default 60)
 *   RETRY=s          keep retrying a lost server for s seconds (default 30)
 *   TIMEOUT=s        seconds per call (default 15)
 *   PORT=n           server port (default 445)
 */
Handler   = L:prismsmb-handler
StackSize = 8192
Priority  = 5
GlobVec   = -1
Startup   = "192.168.1.10/public VOLUME=NAS GUEST"
